    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite (a single acceptance test class, plus its base/helper) passes \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The compile step also confirms the OpenAPI-generated DTOs and MapStruct mappers built cleanly with the new fields.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation for owners. When a create request includes `birthDate` (ISO), the owner's age band is returned on read, computed against `registrationDate`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (`format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` request schema and a read-only `ageBand` string to the `Owner` response schema. These regenerate the `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` at build time; MapStruct wires them by name (`birthDate` in\u2192entity, `ageBand`+`birthDate` entity\u2192out).\n\n2. **`model/OwnerDerivations.java`** \u2014 added a pure `ageBand(birthDate, registrationDate)`: whole-years age via `Period.between`, `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+), and `null` when either date is absent. Follows the existing derivation pattern.\n\n3. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with getter/setter, plus a `@Transient getAgeBand()` delegating to the derivation \u2014 mirroring `getContactPreference()`/`getLocality()`.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added a `birth_date DATE` column so the value persists (tests run hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in `schema.sql`).\n\n**Design notes:**\n- `ageBand` is a plain string (not an enum) to stay consistent with the other derived classification fields (`contactPreference`, `locality`) and avoid an unnecessary String\u2194enum mapping.\n- Age is measured against `registrationDate` (the effective, business-day-rolled date the app already assigns), exactly as the spec states \u2014 not \"now\" \u2014 so the band is stable and reproducible on every read.\n- No band is reported when `birthDate` is absent, per the spec's \"when present\" wording.",
